      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The factor \\( \\ln\\left(2 + \\sin(3x)\\right) \\) is a natural logarithm of \\( 2 + \\sin(3x) \\), which contains a sine of \\( 3x \\), so apply the chain rule from the outside inward: \\( \\left(\\ln\\left(2 + \\sin(3x)\\right)\\right)' = \\frac{3 \\cos{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{\\sin{\\left(3 x \\right)} + 2} \\).",
